Added a declarative Form Layout Framework (`nautobot.core.ui.object_form`, exported via `nautobot.apps.ui`): model forms can now group, order, and conditionally show their fields by declaring `Meta.fieldsets` using `FormPanel`, `FormField`, `InlineFields`, `StaticField`, `TabbedGroups`, `IncludedTemplate`, and `FormSetPanel` components, instead of overriding the `form` block in a template. Fields not named are never dropped; they render in a trailing panel.
Added two visibility mechanisms for form layout components: `render_if` (evaluated once on the server, nothing is emitted when false) and `visible_if` (a small `When`/`AnyOf`/`AllOf`/`Not` condition grammar re-evaluated in the browser as values change and enforced again during server-side validation, where hidden fields are never required and their submitted values are ignored or cleared).
Added `form_panels` contributions from `TenancyForm`, `CustomFieldModelFormMixin`, `RelationshipModelFormMixin`, `NoteModelFormMixin`, and `DynamicGroupModelFormMixin`, so the Tenancy, Custom Fields, Relationships, Notes, Dynamic Groups, and Tags panels are rendered automatically for any form declaring `Meta.fieldsets`; `Contributed(name)` repositions or splices them. Form layout components may also declare `Media` to ship their own JavaScript and CSS via `form.media`.
Added `fieldsets` support to `Job.Meta`, laying out a job's variables on the run form with the same components.
Added the `{% render_form_layout %}` and `{% render_contributed_panels %}` template tags, a `full_width` option to `{% render_field %}`, and the `form_visibility.js` client runtime; Select2 query narrowing now ignores disabled reference fields (including those in inactive tab panes) rather than relying on CSS visibility.
Converted 48 model forms across circuits, cloud, dcim, extras, ipam, tenancy, virtualization, vpn, and wireless to `Meta.fieldsets`, replacing their hand-written form templates (kept as one-line `{% extends %}` shims where Apps may extend them, or trimmed to their remaining `title`/`tabs`/`buttons`/`javascript` blocks). Along the way: the Interface form shows or hides the VLAN fields declaratively based on the 802.1Q mode and now shows its `module_family`/`module` fields; Controller, Module, and Circuit Termination use mutually exclusive tabs (`clear_inactive=True`) in place of per-page scripts; Custom Field validation rules and choices show or hide by type without `customfield_form.js`; and fields that templates had silently omitted are now rendered (`PowerFeed.power_path`, `VRF.virtual_device_contexts`, `Cluster.devices`, `WirelessNetwork.tenant`, VPN Profile tenancy).
Added `Omitted`, `FormField(template_path=...)`, `FormField(as_hidden=True)`, `FormField(optional=True)`, and `TabbedGroups(clear_inactive=True)` to the form layout components, plus `SoftwareImagePanel` (dcim) and `OverridableFormField` (extras) as reusable app-level components that ship their own scripts via `Media`.
Added `RemoteFragment`, a form layout item for a region the server re-renders over HTMX whenever the watched fields change (first used for the Custom Field scope filter), and made `FormSetPanel` initialize `jquery.formset.js` on its own rows (`add_label`, `keep_field_values`), removing the per-template formset script blocks. Select2 widgets now dispatch a native `change` event on every selection change, so HTMX triggers, `visible_if` conditions and plain listeners observe them without per-page bridging; `{% render_form_layout form bare=True %}` renders a layout's items without card chrome, used by the job run page's schedule card. The circuit speed inputs use the `NumberWithSelect` widget with `CircuitSpeedChoices`.
